{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-psa-83-1","title":"Psalms 83:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 A complaint to God of the enemies' conspiracies. 9 A prayer against them that oppress the Church.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3416. B.C. 588. (Title.) A song.Some refer this Psalm to the confederacy against Jehoshaphat, and others to the destruction of Jerusalem by Nebuchadnezzar.</p>\n<p>of Asaph. or, for Asaph. Keep. 28:1; 35:22; 44:23; 50:3; 109:1,2 be not. Isa 42:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-2","title":"Psalms 83:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>For, lo. 2:1,2; 74:4,23; 2Ki 19:28; Isa 37:29; Jer 1:19; Mt 27:24 Ac 4:25-27; 16:22; 17:5; 19:28-41; 21:30; 22:22; 23:10 that hate. 81:15 lifted. 75:4,5; 93:3; Isa 37:23; Da 5:20-23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-3","title":"Psalms 83:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>They. 10:9; 56:6; 64:2; 1Sa 13:19; Isa 7:6,7; Lu 20:20-23 thy hidden. 27:5; 31:20; 91:1; Col 3:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-4","title":"Psalms 83:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>Ex 1:10; Es 3:6-9; Pr 1:12; Jer 11:19; 31:36; Da 7:25; Mt 27:62-66 Ac 4:17; 9:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-5","title":"Psalms 83:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>For. 2:2; Pr 21:30; Isa 7:5-7; 8:9,10; Joh 11:47-53; Ac 23:12,13 Re 17:13; 19:19 consent. Heb. heart. they are. Jos 10:3-5; 2Sa 10:6-8; Isa 7:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-6","title":"Psalms 83:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>The tabernacles.Tents are mentioned because it was the custom of these people, particularly the Ishmaelites, to live a migratory or wandering life; encamping sometimes in one place, and sometimes in another, as they found convenience for themselves and cattle; a custom retained by their descendants to the present day.</p>\n<p>Edom. 2Ch 20:1,10,11 Hagarenes. Ge 25:12-18; 1Ch 5:10,19,20 Hagarites.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-7","title":"Psalms 83:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Gebal. Jos 13:5; Eze 27:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-8","title":"Psalms 83:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>Assur.Assur is the same in the original as Asshur, or Assyria.</p>\n<p>Ge 10:11 Asshur. Ge 25:3 holpen. Heb. been an arm to. Isa 33:2 the children. Ge 19:37,38; De 2:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-9","title":"Psalms 83:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>as unto. Nu 31:7,8; Jud 7:22-25; Isa 9:4; 10:26 as to Sisera. Jud 4:15-24 of Kison.The variations of Kison and Kishon only exists in the translation; the original being uniformly Kishon.</p>\n<p>Jud 5:21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-10","title":"Psalms 83:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Endor. Jos 17:11; 1Sa 28:7 as dung. 2Ki 9:37; Jer 8:2; 16:4; Zep 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-11","title":"Psalms 83:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>Oreb. Jud 7:25 Zebah. Jud 8:12-21</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-12","title":"Psalms 83:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>4; 74:7,8; 2Ch 20:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-13","title":"Psalms 83:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>O my. 22:1; 44:4; 74:11,12 like. Isa 17:12-14 as the. 35:5; 68:1,2; Ex 15:7; Job 13:25; 21:18; Isa 40:24; 41:2; Jer 13:24 Mt 3:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-14","title":"Psalms 83:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>As the fire. Isa 30:33; 33:11,12; 64:1,2; Eze 20:47,48; Mal 4:1 the flame. De 32:22; Na 1:6,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-15","title":"Psalms 83:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>11:6; 50:3; 58:9; Job 9:17; 27:20-23; Isa 28:17; 30:30; Eze 13:11-14 Mt 7:27; Heb 12:18</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-16","title":"Psalms 83:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>6:10; 9:19,20; 34:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-17","title":"Psalms 83:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>35:4,26; 40:14,15; 109:29</p>"},{"id":"tsk-psa-83-18","title":"Psalms 83:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"PSA","chapterStart":83,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":83,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>That men. 9:16; 59:13; 1Ki 18:37; 2Ki 19:19; Isa 5:16; Jer 16:21; Eze 30:19 Eze 38:23 whose. Ge 22:14; Ex 6:3; Isa 42:8 the most. 92:8; Isa 54:5; Da 4:25,32; Mic 4:13; Zec 4:14</p>"}]}